speechtext:
For a copy of the agreement made between the federal district commission and the Ottawa Electric Railway Company in 1929, dealing with the exclusive right to operate motor buses and similar motor vehicles, including sightseeing buses for hire on the driveways of the commission;
Also for a copy of by-law No. 16 of the said commission passed in 1929 concerning the granting of exclusive rights for the operation of motor vehicles for hire;
Also for a copy of any or all orders in council validating or confirming the said agreement and by-law.
